A||||4||Alex2004||Will an s-10 2.8 work with an 84 Fiero?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||06-24-2001||08:25 PM||||My dad has a 2.8 engine out of a 80's something S-10 blazer, he is going to rebuild it, and is wondering if it will work in my 84 without rewiring the whole car, he thinks "Theoreticly" most of the wires will plug right up cept he'll get the wiring harness & computer (i think) out of an s-10, does anyone know if this will work?  He just wants to avoid major re-wiring and stuff. Let me know.<P>Alex...   <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||06-24-2001||08:47 PM||||First the S-10 is RWD, Fiero is basically a FWD in the back of the car, the blocks though from a RWD and FWD are bassically the same except for 2 things:<BR>Starter location<BR>Motor Mount location<P>If you used that block you would have to drill holes on the other side of the engine block to mount the starter and you would have to drill holes in the block for engine mounts.<BR>Also the pre 86' (I think 87or88 they went to TBI) S-10's were carborated so wiring is limited. Because you wont have to worry about fuel injection it should not be to hard, Mainly just starter wires, altenator... For any emmision equipment on the engine i dont know.<P>Kyle<BR>Please correct me if I said somethign false||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||06-24-2001||11:22 PM||||The '87 was definitely fuel-injected (I owned one.)  From memory '86 was the first year for the fuel-injected 2.8L in the S-10; 125HP, 150 ft-lbs torque.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex2004||06-24-2001||11:39 PM||||This one is TBI, i'm still not sure on the year though.  So do you think this should be an easy, minimum wiring engine swap?  LMK<BR>Thanks.<P>Alex...   <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||KRMFiero||06-25-2001||12:08 AM||||Since it is TBI you WILL need the wire harness from the Blazer, I am pretty sure you will need the computer to (you can buy computer for $35 from junk yard) anyone know a way to wire it without using S-10 computer?||||reg||1
